},{"type":"html","id":"ggUjzu7v6FV_text","label":"ggUjzu7v6FV_text","default":"<p>During our checkup my vet asked if I was cleaning my dog's tear stains. She said baby wipes don't remove bacteria and gave me these to try. The stains cleared up in 3 weeks. Should have started sooner.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggPVN_1x1jG_text","label":"ggPVN_1x1jG_text","default":"<p>— <strong>Patricia H., Shih Tzu owner</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggaND8cnrh4_text","label":"ggaND8cnrh4_text","default":"<p>No more vet visits for this</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggdtZsjo2-K_text","label":"ggdtZsjo2-K_text","default":"<p>Used to take my dog to the groomer every month just for the tear stains. Now I do it myself in 30 seconds daily. Saves me time and money, and the results are actually better.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg9uxpfOZ6G_text","label":"gg9uxpfOZ6G_text","default":"<p>— <strong>Susan T., Poodle owner</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCeieA21W2_text","label":"ggCeieA21W2_text","default":"<p><strong>So much easier than I expected</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3ulpiTVoK_text","label":"gg3ulpiTVoK_text","default":"<p>I thought it would be complicated but it's literally just wipe around the eyes once a day. Takes maybe 20 seconds. My dog doesn't even resist. Stains are almost completely gone after 2 weeks.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggOgpQOlJeM_text","label":"ggOgpQOlJeM_text","default":"<p>— <strong>Margaret W., Maltipoo owner</strong></p>"}],
